speechtext:
The amount of $1,200 is asked for by District Engineer Bernasconi to repair the wharf which was seriously damaged by a severe northwesterly storm. Assistant District Engineer MeKean reported on October 9, 1915, as follows:
On October 2nd last I made an examination of the breakwater at Broad Cove Marsh, Inverness county, and found that it had been seriously damaged by a severe north-westerly storm and extra high tide which occurred previous to my visit. On August 20th last, I reported on this work as requiring $500 to place it in good condition. Now it will require $1,200 made up as follows: 320 cubic yards stone ballast, $192; 6,000 feet B.M. 3-inch covering, $150; 1,000 feet B.M. curb timber, $30; 3.000 fenders, $90; 400 lineal feet logs, $80; 50 piles, $200; 400 stringers, $80; 200 braces, $40;	500 pounds iron, $25 ; labour, $200 ;
omissions and contingencies, $113; total,
